Z||000000||horseman||11-11-2000||09:22 AM||||Here is the article where Smokey Yunick built the duke that produced 250HP,230FT/LBS TORQUE,and got over 50MPG.<BR>Go to hotrodarchives.com...then look for article titled "THE NEXT STEP" found in June of 84 issue. Very coool..or should I say HOT?||||reg||6
Z||000001||horseman||11-11-2000||08:28 PM||||I know that from reading the archives of this list that there are some exceptionally bright fiero owners out there. I am very thankful for this as this is my first Fiero.<BR>I bought it for a winter grocery getter but now find myself getting caught up in this car. Thanks in part to all here.<BR>Anyway everyone,even v-6 owners should check out Smokey's article. I just wish I had the engineering skills to pull it off. The possibilities seem incredible.....1.8HP per cubic inch without Nitrous or Turbos or Blowers and no internal machining.Hey V-8 guys; we are talking about 630 HORSES from a normally aspirated chevy 350 running on pump gas with great mileage! Does that get your attention?<BR>Charlie||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||11-12-2000||08:33 PM||||Smokey Yunick developed a concept called "hot vapor" combustion. That's what this article appears to be about. (I read a different, but similar, article.) The technology seemed to make sense to my non-engineering self, at the time. I wonder why it hasn't caught on, though.<P>Raydar||||reg||1
